# Profile: video
# Blocks YouTube for BRICKED CLIENTS ONLY, while deliberately keeping the
# rest of Google (search, Gmail, Drive, Maps, Photos, Android services)
# working. That is why this list names YouTube-specific hosts instead of
# anything broad like googleapis.com or gstatic.com.

# Stop browsers resolving their DNS-over-HTTPS provider, which would let them
# bypass the Pi entirely. See doh-bootstrap.list for what this does and does
# not cover.
@include doh-bootstrap

# --- YouTube front end ---
youtube.com
youtu.be
youtube-nocookie.com
yt.be

# --- YouTube static assets and thumbnails ---
ytimg.com
ggpht.com
                        # ggpht.com serves channel avatars and is used almost
                        # exclusively by YouTube, so it is safe to block here.

# --- YouTube media delivery ---
googlevideo.com
                        # This is the actual video stream CDN. Blocking it is
                        # what stops playback even when the UI partly loads.

# --- YouTube API (narrowly scoped subdomains of googleapis.com) ---
youtubei.googleapis.com
youtubeembeddedplayer.googleapis.com
                        # IMPORTANT: only these two googleapis.com subdomains
                        # are blocked. Never add googleapis.com itself - it
                        # would break Play Store, Maps, sign-in and most
                        # Android and iOS apps on the bricked devices.

# --- YouTube Music ---
music.youtube.com
                        # Already covered by youtube.com above; listed
                        # explicitly so it is obvious it is intended.
